course: dictionary
lesson: 11370
title: Body words: abdominal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abdominal is a word about the tummy. The abdomen is the belly part of the body, between the chest and the hips. «Sam had abdominal pain after lunch.» Pain is hurt, so abdominal pain must be a tummy ache.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Crunches are abdominal exercises.» Crunches are an exercise done lying down, lifting the shoulders off the floor. The clue is in the exercise: it works the tummy muscles, so abdominal must mean to do with the tummy.
explain: Scientists use the word in a different place. In insects, the abdomen is the back part of the body, behind the head and the middle part. «A bee's abdominal stripes are yellow and black.» The context tells you the word is about the back part of the bee, not the tummy of a person.
fact: The abdomen is the belly part of the body, between the chest and the hips.
fact: «Abdominal muscles» are the muscles of the tummy.
fact: «Abs» is an informal, everyday short word for abdominal muscles.
fact: «Abdominal pain» means tummy ache.
fact: In insects, the abdomen is the back part of the body, after the head and thorax.
exercise: «Sam had abdominal pain after lunch.» What does abdominal mean here? | To do with the hands | *To do with the tummy | To do with the head | To do with the feet
exercise: «Crunches are abdominal exercises.» Which part of the body do they work? | Neck | *The tummy | Arms | Legs
exercise: In a bee, which part is the abdomen? | The legs | *The back part of the body | The wings | The head
test: The nurse gently pressed on Mia's abdomen to check for pain. Where is the abdomen? | The top of the head | The shoulders | The knees | *The belly, between the chest and the hips
test: «Abs» is an informal word for what? | *Tummy muscles | Eyelashes | Bones | Fingernails
exam: Which phrase means tummy ache? | *Abdominal pain | Dental muscles | Nasal exercises | Cardiac sprint
